roadmapPhases.goal:
Give every developer persona a governed path:
- testers get the API Lab;
- JS/TS, Python, Java and .NET developers get SDKs;
- ABAP Cloud and on-premise developers get an abapGit SDK and OAuth;
- low-code makers get a Power Platform connector;
- coding agents get a read-only Studio MCP.

This phase also opens update, delete, actions and $batch, about 52k scenarios, tested on the twin first. By the end, the 30-minute time to first call is true for the twin. Estimate: 10 to 12 weeks. Phase 2 can overlap Phase 1 once P1.3 lands.

Make RISE, on-premise S/4 and ECC reachable, and make CoreEdge easy to set up anywhere. These targets account for 228k valid scenarios and are effectively unreachable from the hosted instance today (connection-url-guard.ts:15-33; plain fetch with no agent, tdd-connector.ts:614-627).

This phase adds:
- a customer-held connector that only dials out;
- X.509 and principal propagation to SAP;
- a 15-minute self-host package with KMS, SSO and HA.

Estimate: 12 to 14 weeks.

Remove the two largest blockers by scenario count: non-OData tech (74.2%) and patterns beyond synchronous OData (78.8%). This phase adds:
- SOAP, REST (Ariba, Concur, SuccessFactors REST, BTP services), RFC/BAPI, IDoc and file adapters;
- events with governed webhooks;
- a durable runtime for async writes, flows and bulk jobs;
- declarative mapping;
- Integration Suite as a governed backend for B2B and the long tail.

Every adapter inherits the grants, policy, containment, audit, twin and Lab built in Phases 0 to 3. Estimate: 16 to 20 weeks, and it can be split by demand.

Lead where Integration Suite is weakest in the simulation: AI_AGENT consumers (0% full) and AI_ASSIST and GOVERN at 1. This phase turns CoreEdge's governance into continuous, exportable proof:
- a runtime MCP gateway for agents with human-confirmed writes;
- a grounded Studio copilot;
- behavioural anomaly detection with graded auto-containment;
- an evidence vault with SIEM streaming and evidence packs;
- end-user acting-for with consent;
- the Digital Access estimator.

Estimate: 10 to 12 weeks. P6.1 is gated by the SAP API Policy §2.2.2 legal reading.
